      "writtenOn": "2023-11-07T07:52:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think there is a race here. Here is the scenario :\n\n- A client registers listener id 3 and is enqueued\n- Almost at the same time there is a state change (e.g. DETACHED to CHILD), which enqueues\n- The client registration is sent to ot-daemon with id 3. ot-daemon calls back immediately with id 3 and this is enqueued\n- Then this method is called with id -1, which calls callback with id 3 and state child (because here `hasChange` is true)\n- And then this method is also called with id 3 and state CHILD (so `id \u003d\u003d listenerId`) so you end up calling it twice\n\nSame below\n\n(doesn\u0027t have to be fixed for this patch)",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 663,
        "startChar": 20,
        "endLine": 663,
        "endChar": 75
      },
      "revId": "dcdcd2ec0ce98c644330ff88bc9685818f2a86ee",
